+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+- **Empty Input:** Handled by returning a zero bounding box [S2, unofficial].
+- **Degenerate Covariance:** If all points are collinear or coplanar, the covariance matrix will be singular, causing PCA to fail or produce arbitrary orientations [G].
+- **Precision:** Homogeneous coordinate forcing and matrix inversion can accumulate floating-point errors; use double precision for construction if high accuracy is required [G].
+- **Scale Reciprocal:** The source computes `scale_recip` but does not apply it in the matrix construction; it is retained for potential downstream normalization or inverse transformations [S2, unofficial].
